  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines First Financial Sector Reform Development Policy Financing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the First Financial Sector Reform Development Policy Financing Project in Philippines is to support financial sector reforms to assist the Government of the Philippines in achieving a resilient, inclusive and sustainable financial sector. The first pillar supports reforms aimed at strengthening financial sector stability, integrity and resilience. It supports authorities in addressing significant legal, regulatory, and supervisory gaps to:  (i) allow effective prudential supervision of banks, including conglomerate supervision, (ii) enhance the effectiveness of the anti-money laundering and combating the financing of terrorism regime to reduce reputational risks, (iii) bring the insurance sector legislation in line with international standards and promote sustainable development of the insurance industry, and iv) enhance crisis management and resolution. The second pillar supports reforms to expand financial inclusion for individuals and firms. It supports authorities in accelerating reforms to promote innovative financial services, including the vulnerable, by harnessing digital technologies to expand the reach of the financial sector to underserved segments, strengthening the framework for responsible finance to build consumer trust in the financial sector, and improving the quality of the credit information infrastructure ecosystem to support MSME access to finance during recovery. The third pillar supports reforms to catalyze disaster risk and sustainable finance. It supports authorities in implementing reforms aimed at enhancing public-private partnership-based financial instruments for disaster risk finance and greening the financial sector to support sustainable economic recovery from the COVID-19 crisis. Key reforms include establishing public-private risk pooling mechanisms for catastrophe insurance to support sustainable market development and allow inclusive access to catastrophe insurance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program development objective of this programmatic operation is to support financial sector reforms that will assist the Government of the Philippines in achieving a resilient, inclusive and sustainable financial sector.</narrative>
  </description>
